---
// The privacy notice (SPEC US-X3, §6.6; ROADMAP 4.7): what the chat stores, masking, retention,
// what the browser keeps, no analytics cookies. Static HTML, no JS. Every fact here mirrors the
// code: services/stats.py and services/masking.py (statistics), services/tracing.py (Langfuse),
// services/limits.py (IP addresses in memory only), src/lib/chat (session storage). Wording
// approved by Ivan on 2026-11-05 (ROADMAP 4.7: "C → I review"); a change to any of those files
// that changes a fact here changes this page too. Tests: e2e/privacy.spec.ts.
import PageProse from '../components/PageProse/PageProse.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'ivanvasyunin@gmail.com';
const RETENTION_DAYS = 30;
const UPDATED = '2026-11-05';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Ivan Vasiunin"
  description="What happens to your questions to Elio, what is stored, for how long, and what is not."
>
  <PageProse>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>
      This is Ivan Vasiunin's personal website. The CV (Text mode) works without any data from you.
      This page explains what happens when you ask Elio, the AI assistant, a question.
    </p>

    <h2>When you ask Elio a question</h2>
    <p>
      Your question goes to this site's server. The server sends it, as you wrote it, to OpenAI's
      models, which classify it, find matching parts of Ivan's own materials and write the answer.
      Please don't put personal information in your questions.
    </p>
    <p>Elio is an AI assistant. Its answers can be wrong; Ivan is the source of truth.</p>

    <h2>What the site keeps, and for how long</h2>
    <p>For every answer the server keeps one statistics record:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>when it was;</li>
      <li>
        what kind of question it was (about Ivan, a greeting, off-topic, or an attempt to change
        Elio's rules) and its language;
      </li>
      <li>how the answer ended, how long it took and roughly what it cost;</li>
      <li>
        the question itself, with email addresses, phone numbers and links replaced by placeholders.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>These records are deleted automatically after {RETENTION_DAYS} days.</p>

    <h2>Monitoring</h2>
    <p>
      To find and fix problems, the server sends a trace of each answer (the question, the earlier
      messages of the chat, the parts of Ivan's materials it used and the answer) to Langfuse, a
      monitoring service hosted in the European Union. Email addresses, phone numbers and links are
      replaced by placeholders before anything leaves the server. Langfuse keeps traces for up to
      {RETENTION_DAYS} days.
    </p>
    <p>
      Masking finds what has a recognisable shape. Names, addresses or nicknames have none, so they
      are not masked: another reason to keep them out of your questions.
    </p>

    <h2>What is never stored</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your IP address: it is used only in the server's memory, to limit how many questions can be
        asked in a short time, and it is never written down.
      </li>
      <li>Your name or any account: there are none.</li>
      <li>Your question in the server's logs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What your browser keeps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The conversation with Elio stays in this browser tab (session storage), so it is still there
        when you switch to the CV and back. It is gone when you close the tab, reload the page or
        press "New chat".
      </li>
      <li>Your choice of light or dark theme (local storage).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics or advertising trackers.</p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Write to Ivan at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="page-prose__note">
      Last updated: <time datetime={UPDATED}>{UPDATED}</time>.
    </p>
  </PageProse>
</BaseLayout>
